<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Popular Front (Spain)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Popular Front was an electoral coalition of Spanish left-wing parties, including Republicans, Socialists and Communists, formed in January 1936. It narrowly won the general election of February 1936, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-azana">Manuel Azaña</a> became prime minister and then president of the Republic. Amid rising political violence, a military conspiracy against its government launched the coup of July 1936 that began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/popular-front-spain.jpg" alt="Popular Front (Spain)" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_International_Brigades_(Spain).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
